Full load for files
-------------------

we use Get Metadata activity to get that metadata of the landing zone after that we use for each activity in that
we explicitly un-check the sequential loop because since we are doing full load we need more parallelism ,with sequential check only one file will get at a time other will be in queue, So we explicitly increase batch count
and yes of course inside we use copy activity based on the batch count copy activity will perform the copy

explanation:-
"For a full load of files, I use a Get Metadata activity with a wildcard path to list every file in the landing zone, since full load means processing everything, not just what's new. That feeds into a ForEach activity, and I explicitly uncheck Sequential, because by default ForEach processes one file at a time, with the rest waiting in queue, which would be slow for a full load given the larger volume involved. Instead, I set a higher batch count, so multiple files copy in parallel, each iteration of the loop running its own Copy activity, and the batch count determines how many of those run simultaneously."


[Get Metadata: list ALL files, wildcard path across all folders]
        ↓
[ForEach: Sequential = false, Batch count = 10–20 (or higher, up to 50)]
        ↓
    [Copy activity: landing/{file} → staging, sink Copy behavior = Overwrite]
        ↓ (success)
    [Stored Procedure (optional): log file_name, 'Loaded', 'FULL', timestamp]


